  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1....Quiet through Thursday with high pressure in \ncontrol. \n\nA cold front is moving through currently and will be offshore by \nlate this morning. High pressure begins to move in, resulting in a \nstretch of nice days through at least Thursday. A brief period of \ngusty winds is anticipated later today with gusts upwards of 20 to \n30 MPH expected for the late morning and afternoon hours. Winds will \ndiminish around sunset. Tranquil weather and mostly clear skies will \ncontinue through Thursday.\n\nTemperatures both today and tomorrow will be in the 70s. Lows \ntonight drop into the low to mid 50s with some 40s expected in the \nPoconos and New Jersey. By Wednesday, temperatures climb into above \nnormal temperatures with highs in the low to mid 80s. This stretch \nof above normal temperatures should continue until Friday. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Somewhat unsettled for the end of the week and the \nweekend with multiple systems expected to move through. \n\nA cold front comes in on Thursday Night into Friday, which could \nresult in a few showers moving through. Guidance has backed off on \ncoverage though and now the end of the week looks quiet for most. \nUpper level ridging looks to break down by Saturday though, \nresulting in a more progressive pattern. Still a bit early to \nspeculate on specific impacts but the next chance for widespread \nrainfall appears to be focused Sunday into Monday with a system \nmoving through. Details will come into focus over the coming days on \nwhat, if any, impacts would be.",
